# Buildroot >= 2026.05 moved mosquitto's websocket support into a choice
# (see package/mosquitto/Config.in) that defaults to "none". A plain
# "select" of a choice member from tezuka_tools_mini's Config.in does not
# reliably override that default, so it must be set explicitly here
# instead -- without it the broker builds and starts fine but refuses
# the mosquitto.conf websocket listeners the dashboard depends on.
# See plutoplus_maiasdr_defconfig / commit b7b03a3 for the original fix.
#
# NOTE: an earlier version of this line set WS_BUILTIN instead, on the
# theory that skipping WS_LIBWS would drop libwebsockets and close this
# board's QSPI overflow. Verified wrong via a defconfig-only dry run:
# BR2_PACKAGE_IIO_WS (see package/iio_ws/Config.in) has its own real,
# hard dependency on BR2_PACKAGE_LIBWEBSOCKETS regardless of mosquitto's
# WS choice, so libwebsockets.so.21 (+ LIBWEBSOCKETS_EXT_POLL, which
# defaults to y whenever LIBWEBSOCKETS is on at all) gets built and
# installed either way -- WS_BUILTIN saved nothing. Reverted to
# WS_LIBWS for consistency with the other 13 boards; the actual QSPI
# overflow needs a different fix, tracked separately.
BR2_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO_WS_LIBWS=y
